  "body": "Inference is scheduled separately from overlay drawing and measured with bounded successful-event metrics. Independent review found that deferred work could read a different live image than its arrival key, and that rVFC startup could miss an already-presented first image. The corrections bind an owned immutable input to its source-image timestamp and bootstrap the first usable image through the same latest-only path.\n\n| Frozen binding | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Final HEAD | `f81ce6102ec4f459ef7a0c3fb7e55d126b157be5` |\n| Final tree | `d15536393c00c55c16c8654612d13d8e7e5692a7` |\n| Corrective implementation commit | `89e444820b6befbd333236e65697b5bcf8f5e15a` |\n| Branch / actual base | `fix/inference-scheduler-metrics` → `main` at `f1a0d0bbe343b666c75eae053340ceefc6730d5d` |\n| Reviewed source / independent evidence | `2f4cdea1bc3e6706f49e37116ede8b1881472f7f` / [PR #8](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/pull/8) at `c632cf0cbce82b48503540651120c88fff75c8ef` |\n\n**PR04-F01 — Medium blocking:** accepted. Arrival A previously queued work that consumed live B, then B's notification repeated the inference. Execution now captures the current immutable VideoFrame, uses its intrinsic image timestamp, passes that exact object into the selected SDK task, and closes only the owning job's image. Generation/readiness checks surround capture, work and adoption; capture errors expose a stopped/retry state. The no-VideoFrame compatibility path reconciles execution-time quality/currentTime progress and late notifications, with documented precision limits.\n\n**PR04-F02 — Medium blocking:** accepted. Startup now also reserves the ready image, without waiting for another rVFC event. Bootstrap and racing notifications share consumed-input deduplication. New camera/model sessions accept timestamp zero again; threshold-only changes preserve stale-result rejection. Camera/model ownership and initialization counts are retained.\n\nBoth corrections are in [`89e4448`](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/commit/89e444820b6befbd333236e65697b5bcf8f5e15a). **Both IDs remain pending the separate reviewer's closure confirmation.** No Author check is called independent approval.\n\nValidation on unchanged corrected product/test bytes:\n- Clean locked npm ci, typecheck, lint, **109 unit/component tests**, production build, **all 8 browser cases**, **all 7 CSS/JavaScript fault controls**, working-tree/full-base whitespace checks: exit 0.\n- Original main baseline: **61/61**, using the same locked installation with its original source unchanged.\n- Unmodified independent acceptance vectors: **before 25 pass / 4 fail; after 29/29 pass**.\n- Unmodified native first-frame probe: **before 0 rVFC / 1 fallback; after 1 / 1**.\n- Unmodified six native pixel trials: before duplicates (5 of 6 in this local replay); corrected replay exit 0 with no duplicate observation.\n- Added ordinary-CI native tests reach actual App/Canvas/Engine/SDK input, require image timestamp and full pixel advancement during delayed execution, assert one consumption after delayed notification, and test pre-presented zero-time frames, restart and bootstrap/arrival coalescing. They use native MediaStreams/MediaRecorder/video and a separate explicit test-only SDK build. SDK observation is not a scheduler replacement.\n- Normal production output contains neither SDK probe/gate nor test fault marker; test build remains isolated. No dependency, lockfile, CI requirement, tracking/dictionary/speech-service change or test skip.\n\nFinal-HEAD hosted [CI run 40076315419](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/actions/runs/40076315419) / [verify job 120820304359](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/actions/runs/40076315419/job/120820304359) are **completed/success**, terminal update **2026-10-24 08:02:12 UTC**, targeting exactly `f81ce6102ec4f459ef7a0c3fb7e55d126b157be5`.\n\nReadback verified the run SHA, exact-commit check, every job step and downloaded actual job log. Logs confirm exact checkout, Node **24.19.0** / npm **11.17.0**, **109 tests**, matched Chromium/headless shell **v1248 / Chrome 156.0.8078.4**, **8 browser passes**, and all **7 controls** (two healthy successes and five diagnostic-specific expected child exits 1). Native logs show one immutable `video-frame` SDK input per delayed-image case, and zero-time images processed again after restart, with one model creation across three scenes. No system-browser override was used in hosted CI. Artifact **12553407415** (`playwright-report`) uploaded successfully; digest `sha256:559ecc8be90afa982812dbb8ec15609ef12c49682fa7eaf755d6285c4f1d61df`.\n\nFinal remote HEAD/tree/base, clean working tree, unchanged non-Author branch refs (including PR #8) and local validation source hashes were verified. **Ready for the same separate reviewer to re-review. Both findings still require that reviewer's closure confirmation.** Earlier source-only CI `40075745367` is historical and is not used as this final-HEAD receipt.\n\n[Finding-by-finding response, architecture, before/after commands and re-review focus](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/blob/f81ce6102ec4f459ef7a0c3fb7e55d126b157be5/docs/verification/pr04-corrections.md) · [Correction receipts and unchanged-vector hashes](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/tree/f81ce6102ec4f459ef7a0c3fb7e55d126b157be5/docs/verification/pr04-corrections) · [Original reviewed checkpoint](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/vision-edge/blob/2f4cdea1bc3e6706f49e37116ede8b1881472f7f/docs/verification/pr04.md)\n\nLocal: Linux / Node 24.19.0 / npm 11.9.0 / Playwright 1.64.1 / explicit system Chromium 154.0.8037.57. Matched local download was previously blocked with HTTP 403; hosted matched-browser evidence is separate. All browser inputs and SDK results are synthetic; no physical-camera, real-model/GPU or audible-TTS certification is claimed.\n\nRe-review requested from the same separate reviewer: source-image/SDK identity, exact image/token release, first-frame and bootstrap/arrival races, camera/model/threshold generations, unchanged metric/fault controls and test-only injection isolation. PR04-C01's coverage gap is addressed. PR04-R01 remains the disclosed nonblocking future asynchronous lock-wakeup risk; current production inference is synchronous. Browsers without immutable frame capture retain progress-based precision limits. No Worker migration or PR-05+ work.\n\nPR #8/historical evidence and unrelated branch refs are preserved. No rebase, force-push, merge, auto-merge, deployment or settings change.",
